AIMS AND GOALS:

Decision making processes, and information fusion tools at large, are current=
ly=20
embedded in most Artificial Intelligence applications. As a consequence,=20
systems based on decision making and fusion techniques are becoming pervasive=
.=20
They are currently in use in all kind of environments, from entertainment=20
gadgets to safety-critical or risk management software.

MDAI (Modeling Decisions for Artificial Intelligence) conferences were=20
initiated (Barcelona, 2004; Tsukuba, 2005; Tarragona, 2006) with the aim of=20
providing a forum to researchers for discussing models for decision and=20
information fusion (aggregation operators) as well as computational methods a=
nd=20
criteria for model selection and determination.

PUBLICATION:

Proceedings with accepted papers will be published in the LNAI/LNCS series=20
(Springer-Verlag), and distributed at the conference. Besides, papers, that=20
according to the evaluation of the referees, are not suitable for the LNAI bu=
t=20
that have some merits will be published in separate conference proceedings=20
(CD-ROMS, ISBN 84-00-08306-7 and 84-00-08416-0 in MDAI 2005 and 2006).

